// endpoint_get_detached_work.proto — GetDetachedWork: WHAT KIND of detached
// work one unit left as, and WHETHER the record already holds it as ENDED.
//
// WHY THE SHIM ASKS. A task-stream message names its task but, for every
// subtype except `task_started`, never its kind: a `task_notification` states
// neither `task_type` nor anything else that tells a shell from an agent. The
// shim learns a task's kind only from the start it observed, and forgets it
// once the task settles; a shim that restarted since, or a keep-alive rewind
// that replaced the vendor query (whose replacement re-reports an old
// backgrounded shell as `stopped`), meets a notification it cannot type.
// Refused untyped, every such re-report recorded an ERROR (2026-10-02 onward,
// workspace ship-gns: task `bujbjom65`, eleven re-reports of one shell that had
// ended days before). Typed by the long-standing default instead, a shell's
// re-report would be settled as an AGENT run.
//
// WHY THE STORE CAN ANSWER. The run's `detached_work` row is written from the
// announcement and from the run's own frames, keeps the kind they stated, and
// ends when the run's terminal lands. It is located by its ORIGIN UNIT: the
// spawning call's activity id, which is the `tool_use_id` every task message
// of the run carries (GetRunSettlements reads the same column).
//
// UNSCOPED ON PURPOSE, like GetRunSettlements. The key is the vendor's own call
// id, compared for equality, and no two sessions share one. A lineage scope
// over the row's owner would refuse exactly the runs this lookup exists for:
// a backgrounded subagent's own shells, whose owner no producer observed and
// whose row records none.

